Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Tidal properties of neutron stars in scalar-tensor theories of gravity: \
numerical calculation\
\>", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9016040646283913`*^9, 3.901604079675535*^9}, {
  3.901604115287155*^9, 3.90160412832265*^9}, {3.9138785542798567`*^9, 
  3.913878560819117*^9}, {3.929091041861902*^9, 
  3.9290910449556513`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"132771b1-c939-4dff-862d-\
81cae88f53e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Manuscript authors: Gast\[OAcute]n Creci, Tanja Hinderer, Jan Steinhoff\n\
Manuscript link: https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.11323\nDOI: \
https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.108.124073\nCode author: Gast\[OAcute]n \
Creci\nEmail: g.f.crecikeinbaum@uu.nl\n\nFor the numerical calculation, this \
code uses the equations from the code \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Tidal properties \
of NS in ST- analytical calculation.nb\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], saved as \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]TPNSST_Analytical.m\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\nThe \
resolution of the calculations has been lowered significantly, from 122 \
neutron star configurations to 25, in order to execute in a reasonable amount \
of time. This code uses parallelization when useful through the function \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ParallelTable\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. If there are \
any issues with it, one can simply change the function to \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Table\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].\n\nSome of the plots \
and integrators below are set up for the parameters of the paper: \
\[Beta]=(-4.5,-6) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "\[Infinity]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["10", 
       RowBox[{"-", "3"}]], ",", 
      RowBox[{"2", "*", 
       SuperscriptBox["10", 
        RowBox[{"-", "3"}]]}], ",", 
      SuperscriptBox["10", 
       RowBox[{"-", "6"}]]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c400029-0f90-4aae-a143-d7d6a811c547"],
 ". If changed, this might yield errors due to empty data sets. Please, read \
the list labeling under the subsection \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Extracting \
quantities\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Background \
configuration and resolution\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.901604085585343*^9, 3.9016041072639017`*^9}, {
   3.901604142101695*^9, 3.901604217008264*^9}, {3.901604248858264*^9, 
